          "title": "DNS Resolution and Caching",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Resolution Chain and Records",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Browser cache",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "OS cache",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Resolver",
                    "sub": "caches answer",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Root",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "TLD .com",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Authoritative",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Holds"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`A` / `AAAA`",
                  "IPv4 / IPv6 address"
                ],
                [
                  "`CNAME`",
                  "alias to another name, {red:not at zone apex}"
                ],
                [
                  "`MX`",
                  "mail server"
                ],
                [
                  "`TXT`",
                  "verification, SPF"
                ],
                [
                  "`NS`",
                  "delegation"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. TTL and Negative Caching",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==TTL== per record: how long every cache may keep it",
                "Before a migration {green:lower TTL}: fast cutover",
                "Afterwards {blue:raise TTL}: fewer lookups",
                "==NXDOMAIN== is cached too, per the SOA minimum",
                "A just-created record may stay 'not existing' for a while"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Debug with dig",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "dig example.com +trace",
                "dig @8.8.8.8 example.com A"
              ],
              "note": "+trace shows each hop; @8.8.8.8 bypasses your local resolver"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Still the old answer?",
              "text": "A changed record looks ==old== until the **TTL** expires."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why lower TTL before a migration?** Caches expire fast, so cutover is quick",
                "**Why does a new record not resolve yet?** Cached NXDOMAIN lasts the SOA minimum",
                "**CNAME at the apex?** No: use `A` / `AAAA`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "TCP vs UDP",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "TCP vs UDP",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Transports",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "TCP",
                "UDP"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Connection",
                  "connection-oriented",
                  "connectionless datagrams"
                ],
                [
                  "Order",
                  "ordered",
                  "none"
                ],
                [
                  "Loss",
                  "ACKs + retransmits",
                  "no retransmit"
                ],
                [
                  "Handshake",
                  "SYN, SYN-ACK, ACK",
                  "none"
                ],
                [
                  "Overhead",
                  "higher",
                  "low"
                ],
                [
                  "Used by",
                  "HTTP, databases, SSH",
                  "DNS, video/voice, games, QUIC"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. How TCP Behaves",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "SYN",
                    "sub": "client",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "SYN-ACK",
                    "sub": "server",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ACK",
                    "sub": "client",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Data",
                    "sub": "after 1 RTT",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Flow control}: the ==receiver window== caps data in flight",
                "{purple:Congestion control}: ==slow start== grows the congestion window",
                "A **new connection starts slow** and ramps up",
                "==Head-of-line blocking==: one lost packet stalls all later bytes until retransmitted"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Which One to Pick",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==TCP==: every byte must arrive in order (HTTP, databases, SSH)",
                "==UDP==: fresh data beats complete data",
                "==UDP==: the app handles loss itself (QUIC)"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "TCP = ==reliable== + 1 RTT handshake. UDP = ==fast== + lossy. Reuse TCP connections: every new one pays the handshake and slow start."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "HTTP/1.1 vs HTTP/2 vs HTTP/3 and TLS Cost",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "HTTP/1.1 vs HTTP/2 vs HTTP/3 and TLS Cost",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three HTTP versions",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "HTTP/1.1",
                "HTTP/2",
                "HTTP/3"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Format",
                  "text, keep-alive",
                  "binary frames, HPACK",
                  "binary frames"
                ],
                [
                  "Transport",
                  "TCP",
                  "TCP",
                  "QUIC on UDP"
                ],
                [
                  "Requests",
                  "1 at a time, ~6 connections per host",
                  "many streams, 1 connection",
                  "independent streams"
                ],
                [
                  "Packet loss",
                  "stalls its connection",
                  "TCP HOL stalls **all** streams",
                  "stalls ==only its stream=="
                ],
                [
                  "Network change",
                  "connection drops",
                  "connection drops",
                  "==connection migration== survives"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Handshake cost",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Setup",
                "RTT before data"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "TCP + TLS 1.2",
                  "1 + 2"
                ],
                [
                  "TCP + TLS 1.3",
                  "1 + 1"
                ],
                [
                  "QUIC (HTTP/3)",
                  "==1 total== (transport + TLS 1.3)"
                ],
                [
                  "TLS 1.3 0-RTT resume",
                  "0: data sent immediately"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "0-RTT data is ==replayable==: use only for **idempotent** requests"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Avoid repeating the cost",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Reuse connections== (keep-alive)",
                "Enable TLS ==session resumption==",
                "HTTP/2 **domain sharding** is now an anti-pattern: one connection is enough"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "H2 fixes HTTP-level blocking, not TCP-level. Only ==H3 over QUIC== fixes loss."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
